  "implementation": [
    "BatchedAnalysisGenerator inherits native identity, nonthinking template/tokenization and completion validation. Full canonical TARGET prompts validated before generation; IDs enumerate all units, repeated text retained; consecutive cap8; per-batch4096 token admission and deterministic half splitting; output128 and strict EOS/ordered IDs/integer labels0..9.",
    "Per-batch admission is not a whole-request zero-native guarantee: earlier successful batches are preserved if a later singleton overflows; whole analysis fails with no partial result/fallback/retry.",
    "ObservedBatchedAnalysisGenerator uses MRO to wrap the same algorithm without duplicated observer implementation. Outer deadline clamps partition preparation, observer hooks and every transport; existing extraction runtime and quote/offset/summary rules remain imported.",
    "load_runtime and both service CLIs explicitly select single(default) or batch-v1; health classification metadata binds policy/caps/prompt and grammar hashes; combined launcher requires exact requested metadata and records selection in lifecycle.",
    "Acceptance plan optional analysis_policy is single when absent. An explicit field requires identical registration.policy.analysis_policy, registered plan hash and CI code equality; batch-v1 additionally requires the new adapter code binding. Official CLI has no policy override."
  ],
  "binding_refinements": [
    "Always require src/doctrail/meeting_analysis_batch.py in CODE, including absent-policy legacy single and explicit single. The dependency is unconditionally imported; exact code/CI bindings must include it for every new invocation.",
    "Validation calibration gate must carry a known effective analysis_policy identical to the requested plan. Missing gate analysis_policy means single only. Unknown and single/batch mismatches are rejected before any service factory call."
  ],
